README.md
    1→<div align="center">
    2→  <img src="./assets/logo.png" width="100px" />
    3→  <h1>Linkwarden</h1>
    4→  <h3>Bookmarks, Evolved</h3>
    28→## Intro & motivation
    30→**Linkwarden is a self-hosted, open-source collaborative bookmark manager to collect, read, annotate, and fully preserve what matters, all in one place.**
    32→The objective is to organize useful webpages and articles you find across the web in one place, and since useful webpages can go away (see the inevitability of [Link Rot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Link_rot)), Linkwarden also saves a copy of each webpage as a Screenshot and PDF, ensuring accessibility even if the original content is no longer available.
    34→In addition to preservation, Linkwarden provides a user-friendly reading and annotation experience that blends the simplicity of a “read-it-later” tool with the reliability of a web archive. Whether you’re highlighting key ideas, jotting down thoughts, or revisiting content long after it’s disappeared from the web, Linkwarden keeps your knowledge accessible and organized.
    36→Linkwarden is also designed with collaboration in mind, enabling you to share links with the public and/or collaborate seamlessly with multiple users.
    38→> [!TIP]  
    39→> Our official [Cloud](https://linkwarden.app/#pricing) offering provides the simplest way to begin using Linkwarden and it's the preferred choice for many due to its time-saving benefits. <br> Your subscription supports our hosting infrastructure and ongoing development. <br> Alternatively, if you prefer self-hosting Linkwarden, you can do so by following our [Installation documentation](https://docs.linkwarden.app/self-hosting/installation).
    41→## Features
    …
    43→- 📸 Auto capture a screenshot, PDF, and single html file of each webpage
    44→- 📖 Reader view of the webpage, with the ability to highlight and annotate text
    46→- ✨ Local AI Tagging to automatically tag your links based on their content (optional)
    47→- 📂 Organize links by collection, sub-collection, name, description and multiple tags
    48→- 👥 Collaborate on gathering links in a collection
    49→- 🎛️ Customize the permissions of each member
    50→- 🌐 Share your collected links and preserved formats with the world
    51→- 📱 Native iOS and android mobile apps
    52→- 🔍 Full text search, filter and sort for easy retrieval
    53→- 🌓 Dark/Light mode support
    54→- 🧩 Browser extension (star it [here](https://github.com/linkwarden/browser-extension)!)
    55→- 🔄 Browser Synchronization (using [Floccus](https://floccus.org)!)
    57→- 🔐 SSO integration (Enterprise and Self-hosted users only)
    58→- 🍎 iOS Shortcut to save links to Linkwarden
    59→- 🔑 API keys
    60→- ✅ Bulk actions
    61→- 👥 User administration
    62→- 🌐 Support for other languages (i18n)
    63→- 📁 Image and PDF uploads
    64→- 🎨 Custom icons for links and collections
    65→- 🔔 RSS feed subscription
    66→- ✨ And many more features (literally!)
